        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Bear captured in Japan after multi-day search as attacks rise Asia / Pacific Issued on: 09/06/2026 - 17:34 A bear that roamed the streets of a Japanese city for four days, forcing mass school closures, was caught on June 9, capping a search involving dozens of hunters and police. Bear attacks have been on the rise in Japan. Last week, a bear attack in the northeastern city of Fukushima left at least four people injured, and authorities failed at capturing it. EU set to discuss deportation of Afghan refugees with Taliban 09/06/2026 Europe Kim Jong-Un 'at the top of his game' as North Korea to boost ties with China 09/06/2026 Asia / Pacific 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Armenian election largely seen as 'national referendum on country's direction' 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific 'Democratic backsliding': Armenia's 'extreme polarisation, hate speech, stigmatization' mar election 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Major earthquake kills at least 31 in the Philippines 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific China's Xi Jinping lands in North Korea for rare, high-stakes visit 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Armenia's PM secures win in election 'with highest turnout in a decade' 08/06/2026 Asia / Pacific Armenia's parliamentary election a vote on nation's 'geopolitical future' 07/06/2026 Asia / Pacific"
